    "serial": {
        "baud_rate": 0,
        "comments": "\n{{:media:tenda:w306r_serialpoints.jpg?200|Photo of PCB with markings}}\n\nIn order to de-brick, or install OpenWrt using Method 1, you will need to connect a serial cable to the device. You will need to [[docs:techref:hardware:soldering|solder]] wires to a header, then connect [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial.cables]] device to communicate to the serial port of a computer.\n\n**In Version 2.0:** The pads to solder to are near the CPU on the underside of the circuit board.\\\\\n\nThe serial settings needed are:\n| Rate           | 57600   |\n| Data Bits      | 8       |\n| Stop Bits      | 1       |\n| Parity         | none    |\n| Flow Control   | none    |\n\n-> [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial]] general information about the serial port, serial port cable, etc.\n\n[[.:w306r#dokuwiki__top|TOP]]\n----\n",
